N2  - Introduction: The prevalence of NAFLD is higher in type 2 diabetes patients than in general population. NAFLD has become a major public health problem in India due to rising incidence of obesity & type II diabetes mellitus. Aim: To determine the prevalence of NAFLD in rural& urban patients of Diabetes mellitus & comparison of characteristics of DM patients with & without NAFLD in rural & urban population. Material and methods: Eighty urban and 80 rural diabetes patients were divided into 4 subgroups. Urban diabetes patients with and without NAFLD and rural diabetes patients with and without NAFLD for comparison of following parameters. Age, Sex, Duration of Diabetes, Physical Activity, Diet (Vegetarian/Non- Vegetarian), Anthropometry, Lipid profile, Liver function tests, HbA1c, Blood pressure, C-reactive protein, ESR, Serumferritin, CIMT, Insulin resistance. Results: The study group was divided in urban (n = 80) and rural (n=80). The prevalence of NAFLD in urban diabetes patients was 58.75 % (n = 47) and in rural it was 31.25 % (n=25) (p < 0.05). Comparison of NAFLD positive patients in urban and rural Diabetes patients showed significant differences in patterns of age, duration of DM& hypertension, weight, BMI, waist & hip circumference. A significant positive correlation of non vegetarian diet was found in rural and urban patients of Diabetes with NAFLD as compared to those without NAFLD. Levels of blood pressure, FBS, PPBS, HbA1c, ESR, CRP, lipid profile, serumferritin, fasting insulin, CIMT showed no significant difference in intergroup comparison. Conclusion: Prevalence of NAFLD was significantly higher in urban Diabetes patients than rural. There was a significant difference in anthropometric, demographic and haemodynamic variables in urban and rural group having NAFLD.
